## What was independently checked

The verifier authenticated the graph and all 249 source bodies, literal imports, dependency objects and companion files, selected-context objects, cached objects, command lines, stdout/stderr, auxiliary outputs, receipt identities, actual imported-artifact ledger, namespace-resolution checks and native library bindings. All 246 reused receipt dictionaries are literally equal to their accepted 1,575-module counterparts; all three new receipts are fresh in this run. Aggregate source was reconstructed from the exact selected roots, and complete audit source from those roots plus the unchanged audit template and exact selected-module order.

The full actual import ledger covers 5,363 imported modules and 25,831 artifact records. Verification rehashed 27,662 distinct files, totalling 5,087,083,438 bytes, and streamed every receipt-bound archived native-loader trace back to its exact raw length and SHA-256. Each trace was bound to its completed PASS receipt and its archived bytes, and its observed initialized-library set matched the pinned native-library records. Compiler identity and final native rehash stability passed.

The scripts are byte-for-byte the accepted 1,575-module scripts. The unchanged four-owned-Mathlib mask resolves those four modules to authenticated owned objects while excluding their external counterparts. No empty-owned or one-owned namespace substitution was introduced. The verified compiler flags include `-j1 -t0 -M4096 -Ddebug.skipKernelTC=false`; actual invocation receipts, including aggregate/audit, use the 180-second and 4,096-MiB configured limits. This is not an assertion of an OS address-space limit. The unchanged supervisor reports exit zero, no limit event, a 12-GiB allocation ceiling, an 8-GiB free-space floor and a 512-MiB per-file hard limit. The earlier preflight separately checked the unchanged 20-GiB launch reserve and the 8-MiB preparation envelope.

The first failed source attempt and its terminal diagnostics remain preserved. The proof-only repair adds the existing `state` unfolding, exposes two local list lets, and supplies explicit arguments to `PMF.mem_support_pure_iff`. The revision review established no import, definition, statement or hypothesis change. No failed attempt has been relabelled PASS.

